ant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MITSUI CHEMICALS, INC.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OKADA, KEIJI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>THE LUBRIZOL CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KANESHIGE RYOUSUKE</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OKADA KEIJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KANESHIGE, RYOUSUKE</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OKADA, KEIJI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A lubricant composition characterized in that it comprises a lubricating oil base (A) and an ethylene/C3-20  alpha -olefin copolymer (B), that the content of the copolymer (B) is 1 to 20 wt.%, and that the copolymer (B) has the following properties: (1) the ethylene content (E) is 40 to 77 wt.%, (2) the weight-average molecular weight (Mw) in terms of polystyrene as determined by GPC is 80,000 to 400,000, (3) Mw/Mn is 2.4 or lower, (4) the melting point (Tm) as measured by DSC is 60 DEG C or lower, (5) the ethylene content (E, wt.%) and the melting point (Tm,  DEG C) as measured by DSC satisfy the following relationship (I): 3.31 x E - 186 &gt;/= Tm and (6) the proportion of  alpha - and  beta -carbon atoms (V, %) in the carbon atoms of the backbone and of the long-chain branch(es) if present and the ethylene content (E, wt.%) satisfy the following relationship (II): V &lt;/= 10 - 0.1 x E (II)</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>La présente invention concerne une composition de lubrifiant caractérisée en ce qu'elle comprend (A) une base d'huile de graissage et (B) un copolymère d'éthylène ou d' alpha -oléfine en C3-C20, en ce que la teneur en copolymère (B) est de 1 à 20% massiques, et que le copolymère (B) présente les propriétés suivantes: (1) la teneur en éthylène (E) est de 40 à 77 % massiques, (2) la masse moléculaire moyenne en masse (Mw) rapportée au polystyrène calculée selon GPC est de 80.000 à 400.000, (3) le rapport Mw/Mn n'excède pas 2,4, (4) le point de fusion (Tm) mesuré selon DSC n'excède pas 60 DEG C, (5) la teneur en éthylène (E, en % de la masse) et le point de fusion (Tm, en  DEG C) selon DSC satisfont une relation (I) telle que: 3,31 x E - 186 &gt;/= Tm et (6) les atomes de carbone  alpha - et  beta - (V, en %) dans les atomes de carbone de l'ossature et des ramifications à chaîne longue, lorsqu'elles sont présentes, et la teneur en éthylène (E, en % de la masse) satisfont une relation (II) telle que: V &lt;/= 10 - 0.1 x E.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>